<LayoutPage title="Foldster's Projects — About" description="Who we are">
  <h1>About Foldster's Projects</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    A creator-experience consultancy run by Matt Giallourakis (Foldster) and Dizzy Hellfire out of Fort Lauderdale, Florida.
  </p>

  <p>
    We make tools and experiences for content creators — stream overlays, bots, custom tools, branded merch &mdash; built end-to-end so creators can focus on what they do best. We also publish the tools we build for ourselves as free resources for everyone to use.
  </p>

  <h2>The Thesis</h2>
  <p>
    The creator economy is a mess. It's a patchwork of platforms, tools, and services that don't talk to each other, with high fees, opaque policies, and a lack of ownership for creators. We believe creators deserve better — tools that are built for them, that they own, and that work together seamlessly to bring their brands to life across every surface.
  </p>

  <h2>How We Work</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Free tools</strong> &mdash; Every tool on the site (Demowall, Demodrip, Demosky, Palettope, Emotions.dev) are free for everyone to use. These are tools that I've made for myself as a content creator
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Paid custom builds as revenue</strong> &mdash; When a creator wants the tools tailored to their brand &mdash; or wants the full digital + physical package &mdash; that's the work we charge for. Code shipped is code clients own. No DRM, no subscription lock-in, no recurring fees, except for optional hosting, maintenance, and support.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Transparent pricing</strong> &mdash; Tiers are published on the <a href="/services/">services page</a>, not gatekept behind a "contact us for a quote." We want to make it easy for creators to understand what they can get for their budget, and to choose the right level of service for their needs.
  </p>

  <h2>The Team</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Matt</strong> &mdash; 15 years of code (TypeScript, Kotlin, Python, C/C++, GLSL) across mobile, web, and embedded hardware. Sr. Software Engineer at Ritz-Carlton Yacht Collection by day; consultancy by night and weekend. ME + MS EE background, generative art for fifteen years before that.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Dizzy</strong> &mdash; partner and the physical-side collaborator on Complete Package projects (merch fulfillment, packaging, brand). Currently pursuing an MS in Coastal & Marine Management.
  </p>

